Package: mica-mdev
Version: 1.38.0-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1790638915
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: mica-busybox
Conflicts: udev
Description: Mica OS device nodes without udev
 Device management for a Mica OS root that runs OpenRC (mica-openrc): busybox
 mdev, which mica-busybox already carries, populates /dev from /sys at boot and
 then follows the kernel's uevents as a netlink daemon (mdev -d). /etc/mdev.conf
 gives each node the owner and mode udev's default rules give it, loads the
 driver of a module alias, and mdev loads firmware from /usr/lib/firmware.
 .
 It does not make udev's persistent names (/dev/disk/by-*, /dev/serial/by-*);
 Mica OS finds DATA by PARTUUID through blkid, which needs none of them.
